## Claim
Text: "99% of people recover from COVID-19."
Claim author: Donald Trump
Claim date: October 23, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Does the claim “99% of people recover” refer to survival (not dying) or to a full return to pre-infection health without any lingering symptoms?
Answer: Basedon the search result, the claim “99% of people recover” as made by Trump appears to refer to survival (not dying) rather than a full return to pre-infection health without lingering symptoms. The article notes that Trump said cases are “totally harmless,” and it critiques this by highlighting that even mild cases can lead to long-term health problems such as diabetes, blood clots, and chronic fatigue, indicating that recovery in the sense of full health is not guaranteed.

