### How does the infection fatality rate (IFR), which accounts for undiagnosed asymptomatic cases, compare to the 1% implied by the claim as of October 2020?
Answer: Based on the search result, the global infection fatality rate (IFR) as of October 2020 is estimated at 0.15–0.20% — far lower than the 1% implied by the claim that 99% of people recover. The source explicitly states: "Global infection fatality rate is 0.15-0.20%," indicating that the actual IFR is substantially less than 1%, especially in younger populations (0.03-0.04% for those under 70).

Source URL: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33026101/

